    "result_text": "The build is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented rejection of owner creation when the lower-cased email already belongs to another owner, responding with **409 Conflict**, following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection pattern (mirroring the existing `RequireUniqueTelephone` rule):\n\n1. **`RequireUniqueEmail`** (`rest/function/owner/`) \u2014 new pipeline step. Email is already normalized to trimmed/lower-case form by the existing `RequireOwnerFields` step. It skips the check when email is absent (email is optional) and otherwise throws `DuplicateEmailException` if any existing owner's lower-cased email matches.\n\n2. **`DuplicateEmailException`** \u2014 checked exception (`extends Exception`) so it surfaces as an escalation.\n\n3. **`DuplicateEmailExceptionHandler`** \u2014 responds 409 Conflict via `ProblemDetail`, matching the sibling `DuplicateTelephoneExceptionHandler`.\n\n4. **`...DuplicateEmailException.yml`** escalation wiring to the handler.\n\n5. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted the `uniqueEmail` step (with `govern: [ transaction ]`) into the pipeline between `uniqueTelephone` and `uniqueHousehold`.\n\nThe new acceptance test `coreRejectsDuplicateEmail` and the full suite pass.",
